samstack adapts skills from pstack by Lauren Tan, which is MIT licensed
(https://github.com/cursor/plugins). The licence text is below, and a copy sits
beside each skill that is adapted whole.

Adapted whole, each with its LICENSE beside it:

- reframe, from pstack's reframe
- sharpen, from pstack's sharpen
- writing, from pstack's unslop and technical-writing
- typescript, from pstack's typescript-best-practices
- measuring, from pstack's benchmark-checklist and explain-the-number
- verification-kit, from pstack's create-verification-skill and
  maintain-verification-skill

Adapted in part, as points rewritten into skills of samstack's own:

- code-quality, from pstack's type-system-discipline, boundary-discipline,
  model-the-domain, foundational-thinking, minimize-reader-load,
  make-operations-idempotent and separate-before-serializing-shared-state
- parallelism, from pstack's build-the-lever and sequence-verifiable-units
- stability, from pstack's blast-radius
- testing, from pstack's test-behavior-not-implementation

